<section class="www-v2-section" id="runtime">
  <header class="www-v2-section-head">
    <div>
      <p class="hara-v2-kicker">02 · Runtime</p>
      <h2>The host changes. The language and values remain recognisable.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Java, native, and browser runtimes expose different integration and deployment boundaries. Choose a host deliberately rather than treating one runtime as the language itself.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="www-v2-runtime-picker">
    <div class="www-v2-runtime-nav">
      <span>Runtime host</span>
      <div class="kernel-mode-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Kernel mode">
        <button
          class="kernel-mode-tab"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="kernel-tab-java"
          data-kernel-tab="java"
          aria-selected="true"
          aria-controls="kernel-panel-java"
          tabindex="0"
        ><strong>Java</strong><small>JVM / Truffle</small></button>
        <button
          class="kernel-mode-tab"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="kernel-tab-native"
          data-kernel-tab="native"
          aria-selected="false"
          aria-controls="kernel-panel-native"
          tabindex="-1"
        ><strong>Native</strong><small>Rust / Whole-Wasm</small></button>
        <button
          class="kernel-mode-tab"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="kernel-tab-web"
          data-kernel-tab="web"
          aria-selected="false"
          aria-controls="kernel-panel-web"
          tabindex="-1"
        ><strong>Web</strong><small>Browser / Wasm</small></button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article
      class="www-v2-runtime-panel"
      id="kernel-panel-java"
      role="tabpanel"
      aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-java"
      data-kernel-mode="java"
    >
      <header><code>Java</code><span class="hara-v2-badge">JVM host</span></header>
      <h3>Work inside the Java ecosystem.</h3>
      <p>Run with the Truffle runtime, integrate with Java classes and tools, and target Native Image when a self-contained deployment is useful.</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Engine</dt><dd>Truffle AST / HBC4</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Deployment</dt><dd>JVM or Native Image</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Java systems and tooling</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article
      class="www-v2-runtime-panel"
      id="kernel-panel-native"
      role="tabpanel"
      aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-native"
      data-kernel-mode="native"
      hidden
    >
      <header><code>Native</code><span class="hara-v2-badge">Rust host</span></header>
      <h3>Use the primary high-performance native runtime.</h3>
      <p><b>hara-rust-full</b> prepares whole-function WebAssembly and hosts it natively for tools, services, local applications, and embedded products.</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Engine</dt><dd>Whole-Wasm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Deployment</dt><dd>Native binary or library</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Services, CLIs, embedded hosts</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article
      class="www-v2-runtime-panel"
      id="kernel-panel-web"
      role="tabpanel"
      aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-web"
      data-kernel-mode="web"
      hidden
    >
      <header><code>Web</code><span class="hara-v2-badge">browser host</span></header>
      <h3>Run a Hara kernel in the browser.</h3>
      <p>Start with the interpreter core, then load VM, trace, or whole-Wasm compilation capabilities only when the application needs them.</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Small</dt><dd>Interpreter core</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Full</dt><dd>VM + whole-Wasm compiler</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Learning, tools, browser applications</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
  </div>

  <article class="www-v2-runtime-demo" aria-labelledby="pong-record-title">
    <header>
      <div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Live runtime record</p><h3 id="pong-record-title">Pong · editable Hara canvas program</h3></div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Backend</dt><dd>Browser / Wasm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>examples/studio-backgrounds/src/pong.hal</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Action</dt><dd>Run explicitly</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>
    <p>
      The canvas, state, event handling, and frame loop are one Hara program. The source is loaded into the browser kernel only when this surface mounts.
    </p>
    <div class="www-v2-runtime-demo__mount" data-live-canvas></div>
    <noscript>
      <div class="www-v2-noscript">
        <strong>The live canvas requires JavaScript.</strong>
        <p><a href="https://play.hara-lang.org/">Read the first-game guide instead →</a></p>
      </div>
    </noscript>
    <footer><a href="https://play.hara-lang.org/">Build the first game →</a><a href="/benchmarks/">Compare runtime artifacts →</a></footer>
  </article>
</section>
